# ~amd64 keyword unmask for the dev-qt/* (Qt 6) framework set the graphical
# payloads pull in. Copied ONLY when CAPABLE (the Plasma set's neochat/
# kdeconnect/khelpcenter apps hard-depend on it) OR WANT_CALAMARES (calamares ->
# sys-libs/kpmcore-26.08+ hard-requires >=dev-qt/qtbase-6.11.2) — see the qt6
# case in build-x86-host-stage4.sh's accept_keywords copy loop. Every other role
# stays stable-keyworded.
#
# Incident (issue #223, session 20260831-183101-a9dc56, standalone-unaffiliated
# x86): the tree moved the whole dev-qt set to ~amd64-only 6.11.2, nothing
# pre-seeded it into the target config, and the payload emerge runs with
# --autounmask-keep-keywords=y (keyword decisions stay explicit for a
# reproducible hardened build) — so the ENTIRE image resolution bailed and the
# base payload (grub/dracut/parted/jq/nmcli/Xorg/lightdm/openbox) never merged.
#
# WHY ONE WILDCARD AND NOT A LIST (session 20260907-190340-70b501, role
# standalone-thick): this file used to ENUMERATE the 16 dev-qt packages that
# the #223 build's AUTOUNMASK-PRETEND dump happened to name. That enumeration
# is not a smaller version of the right answer — it is a DIFFERENT, broken one.
# The dev-qt set releases in lockstep and its members depend on each other with
# EXACT-VERSION atoms (~dev-qt/qtbase-${PV}:6, ~dev-qt/qtlanguageserver-${PV}:6,
# =dev-qt/qttools-${PV}[linguist] ...). Unmasking a SUBSET therefore splits the
# set in two: the listed packages float to the newest keyworded release while
# the unlisted ones stay pinned at the stable one, and their exact-version deps
# collide. The 20260907 build died exactly there — qtsensors and qtimageformats
# were absent from the list, resolved to stable 6.11.1, and dragged
# ~dev-qt/qtbase-6.11.1:6 into a graph the other 16 had already pulled to
# 6.11.2:
#     dev-qt/qtbase:6 ... resulting in a slot conflict
#     ~dev-qt/qtbase-6.11.1:6[dbus] required by (dev-qt/qtsensors-6.11.1 ...)
#     ~dev-qt/qtbase-6.11.2:6[...]  required by (dev-qt/qttools-6.11.2 ...)
# and that build's own AUTOUNMASK-PRETEND dump asked for precisely the two
# missing members (=dev-qt/qtsensors-6.11.2 ~amd64,
# =dev-qt/qtimageformats-6.11.2 ~amd64). Re-adding those two by hand would only
# move the fault to the next member the graph grows into — measured on the
# 2026-09-03 tree, the 16-atom list ALSO walls on
# "~dev-qt/qtlanguageserver-6.11.2:6 have been masked", a third member nobody
# had noticed yet.
#
# So the atom below covers the CATEGORY, which is the unit the tree actually
# versions. package.accept_keywords supports the cat/* extended atom (verified
# against this portage: with a stable-only ACCEPT_KEYWORDS, "=dev-qt/
# qtserialport-6.11.2" is "masked by: ~amd64 keyword" without this line and
# merges "[ebuild N ~]" with it). ~amd64 never accepts the **-keyworded 9999
# live ebuilds, so this floats with the newest keyworded release only and does
# NOT pull qt from git. Unversioned for the same reason as the calamares/capable
# files: a =...-6.11.2 pin rots on the next tree bump.
dev-qt/* ~amd64
